  "gaps": [
    "The capture covers more than one program: full requirements for both the BA in Business Administration and the BA in Business Economics, plus only introductory text for the Associate of Arts in Business and the BA in Business Information Systems. This ledger was drafted for the BA in Business Administration. Please confirm the intended program.",
    "The capture never names the credit unit (semester vs. quarter). 'semester' is assumed and should be verified.",
    "9 major credits also satisfy Global Campus Foundations: ECO 203, INF 220 and BUS 340 are marked with '*'. The capture does not say which Foundations courses they replace. As listed, the ledger sums to 129 credits (33 + 48 + 48); the overlap brings it to the 120 required.",
    "The Foundations course sequence is described as 'the standard', and 'Courses may be substituted'. The substitution rules are not stated.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled first and counts toward the 48 elective credits, not toward Foundations.",
    "Students who transfer in fewer than 30 credits also take GEN 104, which counts toward electives.",
    "The capture does not state which listed courses are upper-division. This is needed to verify the minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major.",
    "Residency requirement: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University. The capture does not tie this to specific courses.",
    "Several courses (BUS 308, MGT 302, BUS 401, BUS 402) require the Quantitative Reasoning requirement to be met first. The capture does not define that requirement.",
    "BUS 402 must be taken last in the program.",
    "Transfer concentration option: 12 transfer credits in an approved area may substitute for ECO 203, INF 220, BUS 303 and BUS 340. The detailed guidelines are not in the capture.",
    "Graduation also requires a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University."
  ],
